title: 'pallet-asset-conversion: keep the sender account alive during a swap'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    A swap now holds a sufficient reference on the sender's account while it runs, so that the
    account stays alive for the whole call. If the sender ends the swap with no other reference,
    the account is reaped when the reference is released, as before.

    The amounts, the events and the conditions under which a swap succeeds or fails are
    unchanged.

crates:
- name: pallet-asset-conversion
  bump: patch
